  "title": "Which line outlasts the others? 4 trails, 4 rules, 1 grid",
  "description": "Four lines grow one cell at a time on a 36 x 64 grid and can never cross a trail or a wall. Each follows one simple rule: STRAIGHT turns only when blocked, HUGGER keeps a wall on one hand, SEEKER always heads for the larger open region, RANDOM turns when it feels like it. Every crash clears the board: all trails disappear and the lines that are left carry on from where they are, faster (x1.15 with three left, x2.5 for the last two, plus 5% every three seconds). The last line still moving wins.\nThe counters show how many cells each line can still reach. The run is a real simulation picked from a seed search (seed 2123) and drawn and scored entirely by code, with no footage, samples or stock media.\nWas it your pick?",
